// Expected: the newly catalogued builtins are actually checked.
//
// EXPECT: Argument 1 of 'join'
// EXPECT: Argument 2 of 'join'
// EXPECT: 'sha1_hex'
//
// Until 2026-08-25 forty builtins had NO signature, which does not merely mean
// "arguments unchecked": an uncatalogued call infers as VOID, so every
// downstream use of its result is skipped too. Nothing below was reported.
//
// `join` is the sharpest case — its argument order is separator-FIRST
// (`join("-", xs)`), the opposite of the reflex from Python's `xs.join(sep)`
// reading. Getting it backwards produced no diagnostic at all.

func main() {
    array xs = ["a", "b"];
    print(join(xs, "-"));        // ters sıra: ayırıcı önce gelmeli
    print(sha1_hex(42));         // str bekliyor
}

main();
